<details class="performance-notes" id="periodic-time-rules"><summary>Time rules and data coverage</summary>
  <p>Reviewed Time definitions are applied. Part 1 rules define delivery, including current exclusions and invalidation after reopening. Current Ticket Owner controls ticket results; personal time follows the recorded time-entry user, not its creator or a substituted Ticket Owner. Development classification follows the confirmed activity name; targets remain configurable.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>DTC = latest qualifying completion date minus creation date in calendar days; same-day closure is zero. It includes pauses and is not Start Date age or In Progress cycle time. Priority means current Urgent/Immediate, using existing mapping. The configurable general Tickets target starts at 7 days and priority target at 3; the general DTC population remains all completed tickets.</li>
    <li>Ticket cost compares current positive PM estimates with visible lifetime direct ticket hours through RED on the same available tickets. Earlier work is included; future work dates and child rollups are excluded. This differs from personal logged hours, which use only work dates within RSD–RED. Backdated records can change historical reruns.</li>
    <li>Expected Done owner-hours comparison uses the configured share % of those completed expected tickets' PM estimates. Both sides use matching estimate/time-available tickets. The reconciliation separately retains all known Expected Done hours, including hours on tickets without usable estimates.</li>
    <li>Personal totals include valid visible entries booked to selected users on scoped tickets, even if another person currently owns them. Categories are completed expected, unfinished expected, other, archived, ongoing, On-Hold and unavailable-owner review. Archived/excluded hours are paid effort without delivery credit and remain in total/daily hours. Unlinked entries, excluded trackers, outside projects and invisible issues are outside scope.</li>
    <li>Capacity = configured workdays × each owner's configured daily hours. Reuses current weekdays, holidays, default hours and optional visible weekly-hours mapping. Private/missing/invalid weekly values use the default without disclosure. Total deviation is Actual−Plan. Daily actual divides summed hours by summed owner-workdays; zero workdays is N/A.</li>
    <li>Other work has plan zero and raw P−A. A nonempty expectation fully completed with no debt at RED qualifies that owner's other hours as favorable Extra Work. This is an end-of-period classification, not proof the hours happened after the final expected completion. Team Extra and Unplanned hours remain separate; one owner's extra work does not erase another's shortfall. Raw P−A is kept in audit tables.</li>
    <li>CW/h uses a paired full expectation portfolio with usable current weights, PM estimates and owner-time visibility. Actual = delivered expected weight / logged-user hours on that portfolio, including unfinished work. Plan = expected portfolio weight / (share % × its PM estimate). Both sides exclude unsupported contributors with linked coverage. Zero effort is N/A. Confirmed deviation is Actual−Plan.</li>
    <li>Activity/user donuts use period work dates. Selected-user paid hours and all-contributor expected-package hours are separate scopes. Only existing activities named Development qualify, including project-specific versions; QA, Review, Deployment and other activities remain separate. If none exist, development ratios are unavailable. Observed activity and owner-booked shares are shown by tracker/package owner/logged user. The configurable Development to Total Ticket Time Estimation Ratio starts at 90%. Normal DTC starts at 7 calendar days and priority DTC at 3. Existing nonblank configured overrides are preserved.</li>
    <li>The operating policy is to archive and replace a ticket when ownership must change after developer time was logged. This report preserves recorded users and flags owner changes through the existing extraordinary-ticket audit; it does not block edits, archive tickets or create replacements automatically.</li>
    <li>DTC and ticket-cost trends group the final RED Done population by completion interval. Personal-hour trends use entry work dates. CW/h combines delivered weight in the interval with portfolio hours worked in the interval; its plan is the full-portfolio rate reference. Coverage portfolios are fixed across intervals. Partial weeks/months are labelled; no future points or invented linear allocation.</li>
    <li>Positive deviation is favorable, negative unfavorable, zero neutral. Cost overrun within the existing estimate allowance is amber and beyond it red. Other metrics have no new tolerance. Unavailable targets, permission gaps and invalid time never become healthy zeros. Zero authorized visible entries means zero; negative/nonfinite/invalid time is flagged and excluded from comparisons.</li>
    <li>Team ticket costs and hours sum. DTC uses ticket-weighted durations; daily hours use summed owner-workdays; efficiency divides summed weights by summed effort. Owner averages and ratios are not averaged into team results. Current field/calendar/target edits can change past reports.</li>
  </ul>
</details>
